{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___? I'm Dr. ___ from the medical team. I understand you came in with chest pain and shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve had three episodes of chest pressure this week. It radiates to my left arm, and I’ve been getting winded walking just a block."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have a complex cardiac history—multiple stents, heart failure, diabetes, and you're on warfarin. We’ve reviewed your ER labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had a lot of heart issues over the years. Is this another blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ECG showed some minor changes, but your troponin was normal, which is good—no heart attack right now. However, your INR is 5.7, which is quite high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s not good. I’ve had bleeding issues before. Could that delay anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Because your INR is so high, we can’t do a cardiac catheterization right away. We’ve held your warfarin tonight and will monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get a nuclear stress test to see if there’s any new blockage causing your symptoms. In the meantime, you’re on aspirin, Plavix, and Imdur to help with the chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my blood sugar? I’m on insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was 208, which is elevated but manageable. We’ll continue your home insulin regimen—Glargine and Humalog as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2196-12-08 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want that getting out of control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2196-12-09 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your stress test came back normal—no signs of ischemia. But given your history and ongoing symptoms, cardiology still suspects a significant blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2196-12-09 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the test was normal? I’m confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2196-12-09 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but sometimes symptoms and anatomy don’t fully align. Your echo also looked stable—good heart function. But your INR is coming down, so we may proceed to cath soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2196-12-09 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So they’ll look inside my arteries?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2196-12-09 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. If the INR is safe, we’ll do a cardiac catheterization to check for blockages and possibly place a stent if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2196-12-10 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your INR is now 2.1, which is safe for the procedure. You’re scheduled for cardiac cath tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2196-12-10 07:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will I be awake?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2196-12-10 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s done under local anesthesia. They’ll go through your wrist or groin and use dye to see the arteries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2196-12-10 07:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if they find a blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2196-12-10 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll likely open it with a balloon and place a stent. You’ll stay on Plavix and aspirin afterward to prevent clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2196-12-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, just updating you—your cath is confirmed for tomorrow at noon. We’ll start a heparin drip tonight to keep your blood thin, since you have antiphospholipid syndrome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2196-12-11 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But my INR was high before. Is heparin safe now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2196-12-11 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because we’re bridging carefully. Warfarin is stopped, heparin starts, and after the procedure, we’ll restart warfarin at a lower dose with Lovenox in between."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2196-12-11 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, just back from your procedure. You did well. They found an 80% blockage in the mid-LAD—just after a previous stent—and placed a new drug-eluting stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the other artery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There was a 75% blockage in the OM1 branch. They opened it with balloon angioplasty. No stent was needed there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So both were treated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’re now on dual antiplatelets—Plavix and aspirin—for at least a year to protect the stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve reported feeling better, and your lungs are clearer. We gave one dose of IV furosemide for mild fluid buildup, but no signs of heart failure worsening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2196-12-12 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My legs were a bit swollen, but it’s not bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs look stable. Your hemoglobin improved from 11.8 to 12.4—chronic anemia, but not concerning now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 150 now because of the heparin, but that’s expected. We’ve stopped the drip. You’ll go home on Lovenox twice daily and warfarin 5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lower than before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, from 2 mg to 5 mg daily. It seems counterintuitive, but your previous dose wasn’t controlling your clotting risk well, especially with antiphospholipid syndrome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, okay. I was on 2 mg? That seems low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. So we’re increasing it to 5 mg with close INR follow-up in the anticoagulation clinic next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my heart rate? I’ve been feeling a bit slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had some bradycardia. Your metoprolol was decreased from 200 mg to 150 mg daily to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on that for years. Is it safe to lower it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2196-12-13 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially since you’re on diltiazem too. We want to avoid overly slowing your heart. You’ll follow up with cardiology to reassess."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. You’ve improved significantly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your medications, especially Plavix, aspirin, atorvastatin, and the new warfarin/Lovenox bridge. Take your nitroglycerin if chest pain returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the oxycodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re getting a small supply—15 tablets—since you couldn’t refill before admission. Use only as needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Cardiology in two weeks, anticoagulation clinic next week for INR. Weigh yourself daily—call if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well. Call us if you have chest pain, shortness of breath, or any bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. We’ll see you in follow-up. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your daughter is listed as your healthcare proxy. She has your contact info, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she’s aware and has everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Discharge papers are ready. You’re free to go when you’re set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll get ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your prescriptions and discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2196-12-14 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for her."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2196-12-08 20:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2196-12-14 19:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old man with a history of coronary artery disease, multiple prior stents, heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, type 2 diabetes, antiphospholipid syndrome, and prior pulmonary embolism on warfarin was admitted for worsening dyspnea and episodic chest pain radiating to the left arm. Initial evaluation revealed a supratherapeutic INR of 5.7, normal troponins, and mild metabolic acidosis. Due to high clinical suspicion, a cardiac catheterization was performed after INR normalization, revealing an 80% lesion in the mid-LAD and a 75% lesion in the OM1, which were treated with stent placement and balloon angioplasty, respectively. He was bridged with heparin and transitioned to Lovenox and increased-dose warfarin. Metoprolol was reduced due to bradycardia. He improved symptomatically, was discharged home on dual antiplatelet therapy, adjusted anticoagulation, and home medications, with follow-up planned in cardiology and anticoagulation clinics.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery with unstable angina pectoris",
      "Supratherapeutic INR",
      "Antiphospholipid syndrome",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with unspecified diabetic retinopathy without macular edema",
      "Hypertensive heart disease with heart failure",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Pain, unspecified",
      "Bradycardia, unspecified",
      "Adverse effect of beta-adrenoreceptor antagonists, initial encounter",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Long term (current) use of antithrombotics/antiplatelets",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Presence of coronary angioplasty implant and graft",
      "Family history of ischemic heart disease and other diseases of the circulatory system",
      "Heart failure, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
